# Generated from the artifact catalogue. Do not edit by hand:
# run `afx export-collection` and commit the result.
# Catalogue digest: b550d61b348f
#
# An empty result from this rule means the paths it searched held nothing. It does
# not mean the host is clean. Unverified catalogue entries, relocated data trees and
# the paths listed as not covered below are all reasons a used agent leaves no hit
# here. Where this matters, run the suite's own collector instead: it reads the
# relocation variables and the agents' own state files, which no static rule can.
#
# KAPE is Windows only. 40 of the 624 catalogue artifacts declare
# no Windows path and are therefore outside this target's scope entirely, which is a
# different thing from the per-artifact gaps listed below. For a macOS or Linux
# endpoint use the Velociraptor artifact or this suite's own collector.
#
# Not covered by this rule:
#   a registry key, and this rule addresses files. No rule generated here covers one: query these keys with a KAPE registry target of your own. The suite's own collectors read four of the catalogue's registry entries on a live Windows host and write each as a document in the bundle, so a collection from a live host already carries those; this is the answer for a rule and for the entries the collectors decline. docs/ARTIFACTS.md names them
#     crosscutting.windows_execution_evidence_registry
#     crosscutting.windows_removed_product_registry
#   anchored at a working copy, whose location only the agent's own state file gives: run the suite's collector, which reads it
#     crosscutting.instructions_agents_md
#     crosscutting.instructions_cursor_rules
#     crosscutting.instructions_junie_guidelines
#     crosscutting.instructions_kiro_steering
#     crosscutting.instructions_windsurf_rules
#   reachable only through a relocation variable, which KAPE cannot resolve: read the variable off the endpoint
#     crosscutting.instructions_copilot_instructions
#   some of its paths are anchored at a working copy, whose location only the agent's own state file gives, so those are not in this rule. Its profile and system wide paths are. Run the suite's collector for the rest, which reads that state file
#     crosscutting.hook_scripts
#     crosscutting.instructions_claude_md
#     crosscutting.instructions_clinerules
#     crosscutting.instructions_gemini_md
#     crosscutting.mcp_config_files
Description: AI coding agent artifacts, Cross-cutting evidence
Author: agentforensics
Version: 1.0
Id: e1c81afd-382b-cb1b-baac-ab880604af33
RecreateDirectories: true
Targets:
    -
        Name: crosscutting.hook_scripts
        Category: instructions
        Path: C:\Users\%user%\OneDrive*\Documents\Cline\Hooks
        FileMask: "*"
        Recursive: true
    -
        Name: crosscutting.instructions_claude_md
        Category: project_instructions
        Path: C:\Program Files\ClaudeCode
        FileMask: "CLAUDE.md"
        Recursive: false
    -
        Name: crosscutting.instructions_claude_md
        Category: project_instructions
        Path: C:\Users\%user%\.claude
        FileMask: "CLAUDE.md"
        Recursive: false
    -
        Name: crosscutting.instructions_claude_md
        Category: project_instructions
        Path: C:\Users\%user%\.claude\rules
        FileMask: "*.md"
        Recursive: true
    -
        Name: crosscutting.instructions_clinerules
        Category: project_instructions
        Path: C:\Users\%user%\OneDrive*\Documents\Cline\Rules
        FileMask: "*"
        Recursive: true
